+## Owner correction: the drawing becomes the scene (2026-11-09)
+
+**Uplift changes representation: a printed illustration becomes a complete,
+spatial, playable scene.** Ink is the visual language in both states. Line art
+does not mean that the final scene consists only of floating lines.
+
+The three supplied book images establish three distinct moments:
+
+1. **Printed illustration.** Every mark lies on the page. A perspective drawing
+   may depict a landscape, but the rendered illustration is flat: no raised
+   objects, detached shadows or internal parallax, and no active process yet.
+2. **Transformation.** The depicted objects acquire actual spatial geometry.
+   Preserve recognizable features while surfaces, silhouettes and occlusion emerge.
+   This is a presentation transition, not simulated terrain formation or elapsed
+   physical time. It must not fabricate water transport or a scientific outcome.
+3. **Living scene.** Complete terrain surfaces and relevant objects occupy space
+   above the page. Contours and hatching are marks on those surfaces. The reader
+   manipulates one understandable cause and sees its model-driven consequence.
+   The endpoint must read as a geographical scene even without its contours.
+
+The intended realism is spatial and causal, not photographic: simplified forms,
+ink outlines, hatching, paper-like surfaces and quantity-bearing colour. Depth,
+occlusion and restrained contact shading explain form. Raised contour stacks,
+a tilted map, wireframe or coloured wet-cell plot alone fail this requirement.
+A mesh underneath those effects is insufficient if its complete form is not legible.
+
+The scene stays anchored to the page. Transformation is the entrance to the lesson;
+it need not be the subject or the main ongoing control. Do not select a contour
+lesson merely because contours are an existing engine capability.
+
+Rendering reveals geometry without changing the model. Identify initial terrain as
+an authored/generated initial condition or a process-produced state with provenance;
+the reveal never implies that the landform physically formed during it. Subsequent
+landform evolution remains process-based. Rain marks, if used, derive their rate
+and coverage from the actual rainfall forcing. Water surfaces and flow cues derive
+from the corresponding model fields, not an authored route. Representative rain
+marks do not claim to simulate individual droplets; wetness is not flow velocity.
+
+Reduced motion skips the animation or fades to the same complete 3D endpoint.
+Keyboard users reach equivalent controls. A labelled static fallback remains
+useful but does not establish that the live scene passed acceptance.
+
+## Demo selection is open — discuss before planning
+
+The latest owner request supersedes the contour-first / movable-source sequence
+selected in D-5A. Keep that exploratory work and evidence; it does not authorize
+the next implementation sessions. Wave 5A merged in PR #29 (8069a7f); the older
+status saying implementation had not started was stale.
+
+Discuss one small process illustration with the owner first. Only after agreement
+should its session briefs, scene contracts, scope and evidence plan be revised.
+Do not launch a replacement spike or build the candidate during this correction.
+The eventual two-spread/page-turn gate remains, but must not silently select this
+demo or force its second lesson before the first has been agreed.
+
+**Discussion candidate, not an approved brief:** rainfall onto one small terrain
+patch, visible surface accumulation and runoff toward one outlet. One rainfall
+control would make the input visible in the air and its consequence visible on the
+land. A channel or depression belongs only if it serves that single relationship.
+Groundwater, infiltration, evaporation, vegetation, erosion and an ocean are not
+implied commitments. The water-cycle reference conveys a scene becoming tangible;
+it is not a request to animate the whole diagram. Exact teaching claims, sources,
+terrain provenance, model suitability and validation remain to be settled after
+selection. No new scientific claim is accepted by this candidate description.
 
